  "summary": {
    "status": "DRAFT - not approved",
    "paragraphs": [
      "Harlow & Finch Joinery Ltd is a bespoke timber joinery manufacturer based in Calderwick, incorporated in March 2011. The company employs 31 staff and is owned by its two directors, Eleanor Harlow (60%) and Marcus Finch (40%). It is requesting an increase in its overdraft limit from £150,000 to £220,000 to fund additional timber stock and working capital for a new housing-developer contract.",
      "Revenue rose 15.3% to £2,480,000 in the year ended 31 December 2025 (previous year: £2,150,000). Operating profit also increased, to £174,000 from £162,000 the previous year. Net profit after tax was £109,000 and net assets stood at £604,000 at the year end. The current ratio at 31 December 2025 was 1.40, above the covenant minimum of 1.25.",
      "The facility is secured by a debenture over the company's assets and a personal guarantee from Eleanor Harlow limited to £57,000. Interest cover was 6.0x, against a covenant minimum of 4.0x. Customer concentration has increased: the largest customer, Brackenfield Homes, now accounts for 38% of revenue, up from 27% last year.",
      "Compared with last year's review, two differences were flagged: higher customer concentration and three overdraft excesses in the past 12 months (none in the previous review period). No other material changes were identified. Overall, the company's financial position is stronger than last year on every key measure, supporting approval of the increase on unchanged terms."
    ],
